From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MineAqua <mineaquanettm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 01:03:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] MASpigot Restore knockback profile system

Replaces PandaSpigot's own world-scoped knockback config
(PandaSpigotWorldConfig#knockback, now removed) with MASpigot's
per-player KnockbackProfile system, restoring the exact behaviour
MineAqua's players are used to.

- EntityHuman: knockbackProfile field + getter/setter, and a full
  rewrite of the melee-attack knockback block in attack() that
  recomputes velocity from the target player's KnockbackProfile
  (onePointOne mode, ground/sprint/enchant multipliers, combo mode)
  instead of vanilla/PandaSpigotConfig constants. The
  PrePlayerAttackEntityEvent wrapper PandaSpigot already had around
  attack() is left untouched.
- EntityPlayer: setSprinting() override tracks shouldDealSprintKnockback
  so a fresh sprint-attack gets the profile's sprint knockback bonus.
- EntityLiving: damageEntity()'s hit-delay (noDamageTicks) now reads
  the attacker's/victim's KnockbackProfile#hitDelay for EntityHuman
  targets; the base knockback-on-hit method a(Entity,float,double,double)
  reverts to flat vanilla constants, since it now only applies to
  non-player-vs-player knockback sources (mobs, explosions, etc) -
  player-vs-player melee knockback is fully recomputed in attack().
- CraftPlayer: delegates getKnockbackProfile()/setKnockbackProfile()
  to the handle.
- New us.mineaqua.spigot.server.knockback.KnockbackManager: loads/saves
  named profiles as YAML files under a knockback/ directory, each
  profile is a full independent set of options (hitDelay, onePointOne,
  horizontal/vertical + friction/ground/sprint multipliers, comboMode,
  rod values, etc), with a "default" profile created automatically.
- New us.mineaqua.spigot.server.knockback.KnockbackCommand ("/knockback"):
  create/delete/edit/use/reset/save/save-all sub-commands, registered
  through PaperSpigotConfig's existing (previously unused) command map.
  Unlike the original MASpigot command, "reset" and "save-all" are
  checked before the args.length < 2 guard, since they only take one
  argument - the original placed that check first, so those two
  sub-commands could never actually be invoked.

